---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, channels } from "../data/site";
const li = channels.find((c) => c.name === "LinkedIn")!.href;
---
<Base title="About" description="Who's behind Kshitij's Verse, and why the name has an extra S.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm {site.person}, a Senior Staff AI/ML engineer based in Bengaluru. Kshitij's Verse is my corner
        of the AI universe, where I teach AI the way it's actually built in industry.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have 10 years of experience building AI and machine learning systems: as a data scientist at IBM,
        on clinical and life-sciences data at Exeevo, and as Lead AI/ML Engineer at UnitedHealth Group, where
        I led the team building a RAG and LLM triage assistant that helps nurses assess patients. I'm an
        AWS Certified Solutions Architect (Associate) with an engineering degree from BIT Mesra.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most AI content either sells you a shortcut or assumes you already know the maths. This is neither.
        It's the route I'd give a new engineer on my team, stop by stop from Python to AI agents, turned into
        short lessons you can follow on your phone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Trending things make good teachers too. When a game, a film or a launch has everyone talking,
        I'll use it to explain the AI behind it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sub">Why the extra S?</h2>
      <p>
        Read it as Kshitij's Verse. Or read it as KshitijS, for Kshitij Sharma. Either way, you'll find
        me as <strong>{site.handle}</strong> everywhere.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sub">Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, connect on <a href={li}>LinkedIn</a>,
        or <a href="/chat/">book a chat</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title { font-size: var(--step-3); font-weight: 850; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .prose .lede { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .sub { margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
</style>
